\begin{align*} r (\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) &= r (\cos (-60^\circ) + i \sin (-60^\circ)) \\ z &= |z| (\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) \end{align*}
We have $z = 4 - \sqrt{3} + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})i.$  Then
\begin{align*} r &= \sqrt{(4 - \sqrt{3})^2 + (-1 - 4 \sqrt{3})^2} \\ &= \sqrt{16 - 8 \sqrt{3} + 3 + 1 + 8 \sqrt{3} + 48} \\ &= \sqrt{68} = 2 \sqrt{17}. \end{align*}
